 "04 · Creature AI": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span class=\"tdd-key__tag\">Key point</span>Unreal’s NavMesh only covers walkable ground, so creatures navigate in <mark class=\"hl\">three layers</mark> (Reynolds’ model). It continues my <a href=\"../../flying-ai/\">Flying AI</a>.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">⇢</span>Three layers<span class=\"meta\">Brains set goals · the component moves</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "1 · Decide": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Behavior Tree or State Tree: <em>what do I do?</em>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "2 · Route": "abyss/tdd/",
 "EQS: <em>where is my next free waypoint?</em>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "3 · Swim": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Steering: <em>how do I get there smoothly?</em>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "EQS alone zigzags and stops at each point. Steering alone gets stuck in U-shaped rocks. Together: plans ahead, moves like it’s alive.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Perception trick.</b> Sense settings can’t change at runtime from Blueprint, but the Tuner must change perception live. So the engine perceives wide, and <mark class=\"hl\">each species filters in Blueprint</mark> from its data.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"node__icon\">✦</span>Fish shoal<span class=\"meta\">State Tree</span>": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<mark class=\"hl\">One actor, 30 fish as instances.</mark> The actor is an anchor that steers; the fish follow with boids rules, updated at 30 Hz in one batch.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Shoal states: Cruise, then Flee when a threat comes close, then Regroup when calm, then Cruise": "abyss/tdd/",
