 "Debug layers": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<b>Video scenario.</b> Duplicate the curious creature, rename it <em>Glimmer Ray</em>, make it shyer, give its signal a yellow light, spawn it: <mark class=\"hl\">zero code</mark>.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "How the bridge works": "abyss/tdd/",
 "The bridge registers itself in the channel when play starts and clears it when play ends. The reference is never saved: if it’s empty, the widget shows “Start PIE to spawn”. The same sharing explains live tuning: the creature in play reads the very asset the Details View edits. A new field added to the species class shows up in the tool on its own.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "08 · Risks &amp; debug": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span class=\"tdd-key__tag\">Key point</span><mark class=\"hl\">Every major risk has a fallback</mark> written before it happens. The three that matter most:": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Performance": "abyss/tdd/",
 "30 boids in Blueprint": "abyss/tdd/",
 "≈ 435 neighbour pairs per update.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span>Plan B</span>30 Hz update, a third of the fish per frame, profiling. <mark class=\"hl\">The only valid case for C++</mark>, if measured over budget.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Centrepiece": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Editor ↔ play communication": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Could block the Creature Tuner.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span>Plan B</span>An early spike. Fallback: <mark class=\"hl\">tune in the editor, spawn with a debug key</mark>.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "New system": "abyss/tdd/",
 "State Tree learning curve": "abyss/tdd/",
 "Its API still changes between versions.": "abyss/tdd/",
 "<span>Plan B</span>Shoal kept to 3 states, timeboxed. Fallback: <mark class=\"hl\">an Enum state machine</mark>, same logic.": "abyss/tdd/",
